<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lavanaprasada</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">13th century</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lavanaprasada was a chief of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghel">Vaghela</a> branch of the Chaulukya family of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a>. In the early 13th century he and his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viradhavala">Viradhavala</a> acted as regents and generals for the weak Chaulukya king Bhima II, defending the kingdom against Muslim and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yadava">Yadava</a> attacks from their base at Dholka. Their family took the throne itself under his grandson <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vigraharaja-iv">Visaladeva</a>.</p></div>
